    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0157" n="147" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/10–2749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Strong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-10-27T12:00:00+07:00">October 27,
                            1949—noon.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 27—4:46 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Cantel 1231. October 26, Foreign Minister Yeh said that in interview about 10
                    days ago between Nehru and Chinese Ambassador Koo,<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d169-f1"/> Nehru declared, despite heavy pressure from British,
                    Indian Government would not recognize Chinese Communists for 2 or 3 months at
                    which time Nehru opined Chinese Nationalist regime would be finished. Nehru gave
                    as reason for delay in recognition appreciation Chinese help to India in 1942
                    and past Kuomintang financial and other support to Congress Party.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Strong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d169-f1" n="53" xml:id="d169-f1-content">
                <p>V. K. Wellington Koo, Chinese Ambassador in the United States.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
